Screen	race	Race
#H	Race affects stats, skills, and other character traits.
#O	1	Noldor	Strength +0 · Dexterity +1 · Constitution +2 · Grace +2 · Archery affinity · Blade proficiency	The Noldor are known as the 'Deep-elves', for they are the most learned and inventive of the elven kindreds. They saw the light of the Two Trees in Valinor and gained much in lore and skill. They are tall and lithe, yet so strong of spirit that they can endure vast hardship. Their hair is mostly dark and their eyes grey.
#O	1	Sindar	Strength -1 · Dexterity +1 · Constitution +2 · Grace +1 · Archery affinity · Blade proficiency	The Sindar are the 'Grey-elves' who never saw the blessed light of the Two Trees, but who found an echo of it in their queen, Melian the Maiar. They are less learned and powerful than the Noldor, but have fair voices and are gifted in song.
#O	1	Naugrim	Strength +0 · Dexterity -1 · Constitution +3 · Grace +1 · Archery penalty · Smithing affinity · Axe proficiency	The dwarves are stone-hard and stubborn, fast in friendship and in enmity. They live long, far beyond the span of Men but not for ever. They are short in stature, deep-breasted and stout in the leg, and their beards are long. They were named the 'Naugrim' by the Sindar, meaning 'the stunted people'.
#O	1	Edain	Strength +0 · Dexterity +0 · Constitution +0 · Grace +0	The Edain are the Men of Beleriand. They gained much from dealings with the Noldor, and grew more long lived than their kin beyond the mountains. However, compared to the elves they were more frail, and more easily slain by weapon or mischance. The Edain dwell in the north of Beleriand and help the Noldor to contain Morgoth's power.
